1. POLICY OVERVIEW
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
At BlitzApp, we strive to maintain a dependable and fair scheduling system for 
both sports players and independent venue operators (Stadium and Game Center 
Managers).

This Cancellation & Refund Policy explains how reservations can be cancelled, 
how time slots are released, the financial implications under our on-site 
payment model, and how booking disputes are resolved.


2. HOW CUSTOMER CANCELLATIONS WORK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Customers can cancel active bookings directly inside the mobile application 
before the scheduled match or session:

* Step 1:
  Open the BlitzApp mobile app and navigate to the "Bookings" tab in the 
  bottom navigation bar.

* Step 2:
  Locate the active reservation you wish to cancel and tap the "Cancel Booking" 
  button.

* Step 3:
  Enter a valid cancellation reason (required by the system to inform the 
  venue manager).

* Step 4:
  Confirm the cancellation. The system immediately updates the booking status 
  to "Cancelled", releases the time slot in the database for other players to 
  book, and sends an automated in-app notification to the venue manager.


3. CANCELLATION DEADLINES & FAIR PLAY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Because stadium and game center operators prepare physical pitches specifically 
for your group, please observe good sportsmanship:

* Advance Notice:
  Please cancel as far in advance as possible—ideally at least 2 to 4 hours 
  prior to the match or session—so the venue operator has an opportunity to 
  offer the slot to other teams.

* No-Show Consequences:
  Failing to show up for a confirmed reservation without cancelling in the app 
  is unfair to venue managers and fellow players. Venue managers can file a 
  formal "No-Show Report" through their dashboard. Repeated verified no-show 
  reports will lead to formal administrative warnings or temporary account 
  suspensions (e.g. 24 hours to 7 days).


4. VENUE MANAGER CANCELLATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Circumstances may occasionally arise where a venue manager must cancel a 
confirmed reservation:

* Permissible Reasons:
  Adverse weather conditions (e.g., torrential rain on outdoor pitches), 
  unexpected turf or lighting repairs, emergency facility maintenance, or force 
  majeure events.

* Mandatory Notification:
  When a manager cancels a booking through their dashboard, they must provide an 
  explicit reason. The customer immediately receives an in-app cancellation 
  notification displaying the reason.

* Arbitrary Cancellations Prohibited:
  Managers are strictly prohibited from cancelling confirmed app reservations 
  in order to accept off-platform walk-in groups at higher prices. Doing so 
  violates platform guidelines.


5. PAYMENT & REFUND GUIDELINES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How payments and refunds are handled under our current platform architecture:

* Standard Bookings (On-Site Cash Payment):
  Under the standard BlitzApp workflow, reservations are made without in-app 
  digital charges. Customers pay the stadium or game center operator directly 
  on-site (typically in cash upon arrival in Iraqi Dinars). Because no money is 
  collected or held in escrow by BlitzApp, NO monetary refund is processed 
  through the mobile application.

* Private Off-Platform Deposits:
  If you and a venue manager agreed to a private advance deposit outside the 
  application, any refund or credit voucher is strictly governed by the private 
  agreement between you and the venue manager.


6. EXCEPTIONAL CIRCUMSTANCES & DISPUTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
If you believe a venue manager has wrongfully cancelled your booking, demanded 
a price higher than the agreed in-app rate, or falsely reported a no-show, 
please contact platform administration:

* How to Dispute:
  Navigate to Profile > Contact Us or reach out via email at 
  blitz.platform.app@gmail.com. Include your booking date, time, venue name, and 
  a description of the issue.

* Investigation:
  Platform administration audits server transaction logs and cancellation 
  timestamps to resolve grievances fairly.


